      },
      walkthrough = "Quest Started By: | Description:\n**Where:**\n- Skyfire Mountains [RoS]\n**Who:**\n- Gelidalin Stormsinger [ _Quests_]\nRating:\n0/1**_\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*__\\*_**\n(From 1 rating)\nInformation:\n**Level:** | 95\n**Maximum Level:** | 125\n**Monster Mission:** | No\n**Repeatable:** | Yes\n**Can Be Shrouded?:** | No\n**Quest Type:** | Quest\n**Quest Goal:**\n- Advancement\n- Experience\n- Loot\n- Money\n**Quest Items:**\n- Grey Crystal [item=132259]\n- Hardened Stone [item=132556]\n- Lava-Hardened Stone [item=132597]\n**Related Zones:**\n- Veeshan's Peak [RoS]\n**Related Quests:**\n- Bane Bound [quest=8902]\n- For My Information [quest=8852]\n- Partisan of Veeshan's Peak [quest=8932]\n- Testing the Waters [quest=8843]\n- The Dragons' Graveyard [quest=8849]\n- The Orb of Fire [quest=8898]\n- The Orb of Luclin [quest=8893]\n- What Makes a Scorpiki? [quest=8853]\n**Era:** | !Ring of Scale\nRecommended:\n**Group Size:** | Solo\n**Min. # of Players:** | 1\n**Max. # of Players:** | 6\n**Appropriate Classes:**\n- All\n**Appropriate Races:**\n- All\nEntered: Thu Nov 30 23:06:27 2017\nModified: Tue Dec 5 05:21:04 2023 | | **Prerequisite Quests:** Testing the Waters [quest=8843], For My Information [quest=8852], What Makes a Scorpiki? [quest=8853], The Dragons' Graveyard [quest=8849], The Orb of Luclin [quest=8893], The Orb of Fire, State of the Sarnak, The Fereth, Chokidai Unbound, The Arisen, Trial of Discovery, Lay the Trap, Who is Buried in Sathir's Tomb?, Bane Bound [quest=8902].\nFind Gelidalin Stormsinger in Skyfire Mountains in the Combine encampment in the southwest corner of the zone.\nYou say, 'Hail, Gelidalin Stormsinger'\nGelidalin Stormsinger says, 'Ah, wonderful. I have need of a hero. You are one of Norrath's heroes, [correct]?'\nYou say, 'correct'\nGelidalin Stormsinger says, 'Great! You are, I am sure, aware that there is likely to be a conflagration soon. The Combine are very angry with Talendor and his sarnak. I am certain that they will use their power, and heroes such as you, to deal a devastating blow against the Ring of Scale. Before that happens there are a few things that could be done to [help] everyone.'\nYou say, 'help'\nGelidalin Stormsinger says, 'Well I have discovered several routes that I can see to ensuring that not all things are [lost] after the conflict. There is at least one ancient [mystery] in that grand temple that I would hate to leave unexplored before the battles begin in earnest. I may even have discovered a way to gain a [leg up] in the coming battle. Of course I cannot do this myself, I am but a humble musician and story teller. I need the [assistance] of a hero.'\nYou say, 'assistance'\nGelidalin Stormsinger says, 'I don't have anything in mind for you to do at the moment.'\nYou have been assigned the task 'Singing Stone'.\n\n---\n\n1\\. Find the singing stone in Veeshan's Peak and give it to Gelidalin. 0/1 Skyfire Mountians\nLava-hardened Stone is a ground spawn in the lava that looks like a rock. At zone-in room look NE between the two exits,it moves so it may not be in the same spot. Keep in mind the lava does do damage, and be invis to not aggro the basilisk. Also try Jump in the lava with no lev - while floating at the top layer of lava, scroll in to 1st person view - you can now see the ground underneath the lava without the lava interfering. Scan for stone,\nReturn to and Turn it in to Gelidalin.\n2\\. Find the singing stone in Veeshan's Peak. 0/1 (Veeshan's Peak)\nGrey Crystal will be put on your cursor after killing basilisk or wyvern mobs and (a primeval chromatic skywing) in a specific area. (north Island surrounded by Lava room).\n3\\. Give the Singing Stone to Gelidalin. 0/1 (Skyfire Mountains)\nReturn to and Turn it in to Gelidalin.\n4\\. Find the Singing Stone in Veeshan's Peak and give it to Gelidalin. 0/1 (Veeshan's Peak)\nThis phase can take over an hour to update.. Confirmed ways to update it in less than a minute: A) Swim around SLOWLY in the lava in the NW part of bridge room, NOT Kluzen's room. When you get emotes \" You hear a faint hissing sound carrying through the lava.\" and \"The hissing seems very close now. \", stop immediately, wait and look around the lava for a rock (Hardened Stone), this is a ground spawn in the lava around where you were emoted. Keep in mind the lava does do damage. B) Cast invisibility, jump down to lava from the eastern side of the bridge. C) Jump down to lava from /loc 1890, 880.\nRogues can do this part fast solo, no killing required.\n\n---\n\nReward(s):\n425 platinum\nYou gain Experince!",
